# Contracts Integration
RULE: Use unified-api-contracts for external APIs (Databento, CCXT, Tardis). Import internal schemas (pubsub, lifecycle, features, ML, risk, events) from unified-internal-contracts only — never from unified_api_contracts.internal.
UAC is the **normalization layer** — raw venue responses must be normalized via UAC before interfaces return data to services. Interfaces are **venue routers** — they select venue but always return canonical types, never raw.
WHY: Type safety, VCR mocks for testing, canonical format normalization, contract validation; internal SSOT is UIC.
CODEX: 02-data/contracts-scope-and-layout.md, 05-infrastructure/contracts-integration.md, 02-data/vcr-cassette-ownership.md
DO: Import internal schemas from unified_internal_contracts; use unified-api-contracts for external + normalised; use UAC normalizers (normalize_*) to convert validated raw schemas to canonical types before returning from adapters; use VCR cassette path from unified-api-contracts (unified_api_contracts_external/<venue>/mocks/). VCR and live validation are done in the six interfaces (unified-market-interface, unified-trade-execution-interface, unified-sports-execution-interface, unified-reference-data-interface, unified-position-interface, unified-cloud-interface); they hold keys.

TYPED RESPONSE MODELS AT API BOUNDARIES:
  Every adapter that calls an external API MUST define Pydantic response models for that API's responses.
  Pattern: raw dict from response.json() → cast(dict[str, object], ...) → MyResponseModel.model_validate(raw)
  Then access typed attributes (model.field) instead of untyped dict access (raw["field"] or raw.get("field", {})).
  See: no-type-any-use-specific.mdc for full pattern and exemplars.
  Quality gates now BLOCK dict[str, Any] and raw response.json() without model_validate().

DOMAIN SCHEMA PLACEMENT:
  Domain data schemas (BaseModel, TypedDict, dataclass used as cross-repo contracts) belong in UIC under
  `domain/<service-name>/`. Services import domain schemas from UIC; they never define them locally.
  Exception: `SchemaDefinition`/`ColumnSchema` (parquet infrastructure) stays in service `schemas/output_schemas.py`.
  See: imports/service-domain-schema-in-uic.mdc

ADAPTER-PRIVATE MODELS ARE NOT EXEMPT:
  `_<venue>_models.py` files in interface adapters parse external API responses — they ARE external API schemas.
  They must move to `unified-api-contracts/unified_api_contracts_external/<venue>/schemas.py`.
  "Private" prefix does not exempt them from the UAC placement rule.
  Current known violations: unified-sports-execution-interface/_matchbook_models.py, _smarkets_models.py, _betdaq_models.py etc.
  RESOLVED: unified-market-interface/_deribit_models.py, /_defi_graph_models.py → migrated to UAC (P3 #17 complete).

NEVER: from unified_api_contracts.internal import (use unified_internal_contracts); duplicate schema definitions; skip contract validation; hardcode API response parsing; use dict[str, Any] for API responses; pass raw venue responses through to services without UAC normalization; define Pydantic domain contracts in service repos instead of UIC; keep adapter-private models in interface repos instead of moving to UAC
